data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Compute the reward-to-go with the backward recurrence $G_t = r_t + \\gamma G_{t+1}$, where $G$ is\nzero after the last step. If a baseline is requested, subtract the mean over episodes at each step\nfrom $G$. Take a log-softmax of the logits over the action axis, pick out the log-probability of\neach taken action, multiply by the advantage, sum, negate and divide by the number of episodes."},"hints_note":null}

